## 12. Architecture Review Checklist

Before approving the solution, confirm:

- [ ] Merchant business model and billing obligation are documented.
- [ ] Integration model is selected and justified.
- [ ] System context and component responsibilities are agreed.
- [ ] Customer and billing identifiers are mapped.
- [ ] Amount calculation and schedule ownership are defined.
- [ ] Payment authorization requirements are confirmed.
- [ ] API contracts are verified against official documentation.
- [ ] Webhook and status synchronization behavior is confirmed.
- [ ] Duplicate and timeout handling is designed.
- [ ] Failure recovery and reconciliation ownership are assigned.
- [ ] Fulfillment and entitlement decisions remain with the correct merchant system.
- [ ] Security and data protection requirements are reviewed.
- [ ] Country-specific availability is confirmed.
- [ ] Testing and go-live acceptance criteria are documented.

## 13. Known Gaps and Validation Boundaries

The following should not be assumed to be native FlexiBill capabilities without explicit confirmation:

- Real-time usage metering and aggregation.
- Wallet and entitlement management.
- Universal plan-change and proration APIs.
- Native multi-product and add-on orchestration.
- Customer or account hierarchy.
- Consolidated invoicing across multiple obligations.
- Global tax and currency orchestration.
- Revenue recognition and accounting automation.
- Universal cross-country payment authorization portability.

Where these are required, define a merchant-owned component, integration dependency, confirmed product capability, or future product requirement.

